  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Migratie in Belgi\u00eb in 21 vragen en antwoorden (2018), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 4 times. Beyond that, it is used in teaching.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Migratie in Belgi\u00eb in 21 vragen en antwoorden by Jean-Michel Lafleur and Abdeslam Marfouk was published by Leuven University Press in 2018. Conceptually, the work connects to Philosophy.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 4 citations. Citations peaked in 2021 with 2 citing works. Notable citing venues include Language Testing, Ageing International and Frontiers in Medicine. Of 11 citation statements scite has classified, 1 support its claims, 7 mention it in passing, and none contradict it. The citing works include 3 journal articles and 1 book chapter. The citing authors are based in Belgium.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture. It has been downloaded 52 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Reduced inequalities among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by Koning Boudewijnstichting.</p>",
